fetch.py downloads NIST's archive of STEP files, unmodified, and unpacks its STEP files into
ap203/, ap203-pmi/ and ap242/. This repository holds none of them. validation.json lists the volume
and area each file's exporter states in it.

Archive
  NIST-PMI-STEP-Files.zip, SHA-256
  8fa78429e6d8d9b0d7681d223b6aa9ec98c3772185c55b1a0e3679b21c181911
  fetch.py reads it from a copy at cdn.springcraft.ai, or from NIST, and accepts only that hash.

Source
  NIST-PMI-STEP-Files.zip, downloaded 2026-11-08 from
  https://www.nist.gov/document/nist-pmi-step-files
  (https://www.nist.gov/system/files/documents/noindex/2024/06/19/NIST-PMI-STEP-Files.zip)

  The test cases were developed by the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST)
  MBE PMI Validation and Conformance Testing Project:
  https://www.nist.gov/el/systems-integration-division-73400/mbe-pmi-validation-and-conformance-testing

